1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,060
Busan stretches a long way along the coast.

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,400
Trying to cross the city all day can turn

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,920
a lovely visit into a transport marathon.

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,920
Here’s a simpler plan:

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:14,480
start at a temple above the sea

6
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,040
spend the middle of the day at Haeundae Beach

7
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:19,700
then slow down in a Korean spa.

8
00:00:20,058 --> 00:00:23,338
This route stays on the east side of Busan.

9
00:00:23,338 --> 00:00:25,998
You’ll travel north-east in the morning

10
00:00:25,998 --> 00:00:28,598
return to Haeundae for the beach and lunch

11
00:00:28,598 --> 00:00:31,358
and finish nearby in Centum City before

12
00:00:31,358 --> 00:00:33,238
heading back to the sea for dinner.

13
00:00:33,564 --> 00:00:36,444
You don’t need to see every corner of Busan

14
00:00:36,444 --> 00:00:38,184
in one day.

15
00:00:38,184 --> 00:00:40,304
Give yourself time to enjoy each stop

16
00:00:40,304 --> 00:00:43,264
and check current opening hours and transport

17
00:00:43,264 --> 00:00:45,224
routes before you set out.

18
00:00:45,582 --> 00:00:47,722
If you’re arriving from Seoul

19
00:00:47,722 --> 00:00:50,602
the KTX from Seoul Station to Busan Station

20
00:00:50,602 --> 00:00:53,362
takes about two and a half hours.

21
00:00:53,362 --> 00:00:55,762
But Busan Station is on the other side of

22
00:00:55,762 --> 00:00:57,722
the city from Haeundae.

23
00:00:57,722 --> 00:01:01,002
Allow about an hour to reach Haeundae by subway

24
00:01:01,002 --> 00:01:03,322
changing from Line One to Line Two.

25
00:01:03,322 --> 00:01:05,082
For an easier start

26
00:01:05,082 --> 00:01:07,382
consider staying near Haeundae the night before.

27
00:01:07,848 --> 00:01:11,008
Your Seoul transit card also works on Busan’s

28
00:01:11,008 --> 00:01:13,208
subway and buses.

29
00:01:13,208 --> 00:01:15,208
Keep it handy for getting around town

30
00:01:15,208 --> 00:01:17,428
but remember that the simplest way to reach

31
00:01:17,428 --> 00:01:21,008
Haedong Yonggungsa from Haeundae is usually a taxi.

32
00:01:21,546 --> 00:01:23,193
For current directions

33
00:01:23,193 --> 00:01:25,266
check Naver Map or KakaoMap.

34
00:01:25,266 --> 00:01:28,986
They can show local bus routes to the temple, too.

35
00:01:28,986 --> 00:01:30,510
If you take a taxi

36
00:01:30,510 --> 00:01:33,377
show the driver the Korean name, 해동용궁사

37
00:01:33,377 --> 00:01:35,506
or use the Kakao T app.

38
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:39,267
Check opening hours on a map app on the day

39
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:42,066
especially for SPA LAND and the Haeundae

40
00:01:42,066 --> 00:01:43,058
Blueline Park.

41
00:01:43,058 --> 00:01:45,682
The temple gets busy from mid-morning

42
00:01:45,682 --> 00:01:48,131
so an early start is a good idea.

43
00:01:48,131 --> 00:01:51,580
Summer weekends at Haeundae are busy as well.

44
00:01:52,014 --> 00:01:54,434
Here’s the day in order:

45
00:01:54,434 --> 00:01:55,754
Haedong Yonggungsa

46
00:01:55,754 --> 00:01:57,754
Haeundae Beach and its market

47
00:01:57,754 --> 00:02:00,254
then SPA LAND in Centum City.

48
00:02:00,254 --> 00:02:02,334
Finish with dinner back in Haeundae.

49
00:02:02,334 --> 00:02:03,814
The temple is the outlier

50
00:02:03,814 --> 00:02:06,294
so take a taxi or check the current local

51
00:02:06,294 --> 00:02:07,474
bus route.

52
00:02:07,474 --> 00:02:08,094
After that

53
00:02:08,094 --> 00:02:10,814
the stops stay close to this side of the city.

54
00:02:11,232 --> 00:02:13,952
Begin at Haedong Yonggungsa

55
00:02:13,952 --> 00:02:16,052
in Gijang

56
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:17,752
north-east of Haeundae.

57
00:02:17,752 --> 00:02:21,412
This Buddhist temple sits on rocks above the sea

58
00:02:21,412 --> 00:02:23,352
rather than tucked into the mountains like

59
00:02:23,352 --> 00:02:25,072
many Korean temples.

60
00:02:25,072 --> 00:02:28,552
That seaside setting is what makes it special.

61
00:02:28,552 --> 00:02:29,472
From Haeundae

62
00:02:29,472 --> 00:02:32,372
a taxi takes around twenty to thirty minutes

63
00:02:32,372 --> 00:02:33,912
depending on traffic.

64
00:02:33,912 --> 00:02:35,452
Local buses also run

65
00:02:35,452 --> 00:02:37,932
so check the current route before leaving.

66
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:40,970
Allow about an hour to look around.

67
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:43,564
Steps lead down to the main hall

68
00:02:43,564 --> 00:02:45,019
so take your time.

69
00:02:45,019 --> 00:02:47,739
This is an active place of worship:

70
00:02:47,739 --> 00:02:51,028
keep your voice low and be considerate when

71
00:02:51,028 --> 00:02:52,103
taking photos.

72
00:02:52,103 --> 00:02:55,393
Going early also helps you avoid the busier

73
00:02:55,393 --> 00:02:56,785
mid-morning period.

74
00:02:56,785 --> 00:03:00,264
If you’d rather wake up closer to the temple

75
00:03:00,264 --> 00:03:03,869
the Osiria area has resorts and an outlet mall

76
00:03:03,869 --> 00:03:06,510
including Ananti at Busan Cove.

77
00:03:07,116 --> 00:03:07,510
Next

78
00:03:07,510 --> 00:03:09,201
return to Haeundae Beach.

79
00:03:09,201 --> 00:03:11,172
It’s Busan’s best-known beach

80
00:03:11,172 --> 00:03:13,764
and a good place to walk on the sand

81
00:03:13,764 --> 00:03:15,341
or along the promenade.

82
00:03:15,341 --> 00:03:16,750
On a summer weekend

83
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:18,271
expect it to be busy.

84
00:03:18,271 --> 00:03:21,426
Starting early at the temple lets you keep the

85
00:03:21,426 --> 00:03:23,567
beach for later in the morning

86
00:03:23,567 --> 00:03:26,496
rather than arriving at the busiest part of

87
00:03:26,496 --> 00:03:27,416
the day.

88
00:03:28,086 --> 00:03:28,825
For lunch

89
00:03:28,825 --> 00:03:31,498
head into the streets behind the beach.

90
00:03:31,498 --> 00:03:34,397
Haeundae Traditional Market is a short walk

91
00:03:34,397 --> 00:03:37,752
from the sand and makes an easy stop for snacks.

92
00:03:37,752 --> 00:03:40,709
Look for familiar street-food favourites like

93
00:03:40,709 --> 00:03:42,471
fish cakes and tteokbokki.

94
00:03:42,471 --> 00:03:44,632
You can keep lunch casual here

95
00:03:44,632 --> 00:03:47,816
then leave room in the afternoon for a longer

96
00:03:47,816 --> 00:03:49,026
slower break.

97
00:03:49,344 --> 00:03:51,043
If you have extra time

98
00:03:51,043 --> 00:03:53,503
consider the Haeundae Blueline Park.

99
00:03:53,503 --> 00:03:56,667
Its beach train and small sky capsules follow

100
00:03:56,667 --> 00:03:59,244
the old coastal railway between Mipo

101
00:03:59,244 --> 00:04:01,470
near the end of Haeundae Beach

102
00:04:01,470 --> 00:04:02,525
and Cheongsapo.

103
00:04:02,525 --> 00:04:04,458
This is an optional add-on

104
00:04:04,458 --> 00:04:06,450
not a must for a full day.

105
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:09,613
Tickets for the sky capsules can sell out at

106
00:04:09,613 --> 00:04:10,433
busy times

107
00:04:10,433 --> 00:04:13,604
so book ahead in summer and on weekends.

108
00:04:14,058 --> 00:04:15,338
In the afternoon

109
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:19,738
take Line Two one stop from Haeundae to Centum City.

110
00:04:19,738 --> 00:04:22,418
SPA LAND is inside Shinsegae Centum City

111
00:04:22,418 --> 00:04:23,918
department store.

112
00:04:23,918 --> 00:04:27,338
It has hot-spring baths and themed rest rooms

113
00:04:27,338 --> 00:04:29,458
and it offers a comfortable introduction to

114
00:04:29,458 --> 00:04:31,638
Korean bathhouse culture.

115
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:33,618
Check current details before you go.

116
00:04:33,618 --> 00:04:34,978
If the weather turns

117
00:04:34,978 --> 00:04:37,338
the same building also gives you an indoor

118
00:04:37,338 --> 00:04:38,418
shopping option.

119
00:04:38,724 --> 00:04:41,864
Return to Haeundae for dinner.

120
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:43,944
Ribs of Legend Haeundae is close to the beach

121
00:04:43,944 --> 00:04:47,484
and serves Korean grilled ribs.

122
00:04:47,484 --> 00:04:48,424
After dinner

123
00:04:48,424 --> 00:04:50,124
keep it simple with a walk along the beach

124
00:04:50,124 --> 00:04:51,304
at night.

125
00:04:51,304 --> 00:04:51,664
Or

126
00:04:51,664 --> 00:04:53,944
if you’d like to see another stretch of coast

127
00:04:53,944 --> 00:04:56,664
take a short taxi ride to Gwangalli Beach

128
00:04:56,664 --> 00:04:59,164
where Gwangan Bridge is lit up after dark.

129
00:04:59,622 --> 00:05:02,674
The main transport decision is how to get to

130
00:05:02,674 --> 00:05:03,465
the temple.

131
00:05:03,465 --> 00:05:06,404
A taxi from Haeundae takes around twenty to

132
00:05:06,404 --> 00:05:07,421
thirty minutes

133
00:05:07,421 --> 00:05:08,834
depending on traffic

134
00:05:08,834 --> 00:05:10,642
and is the easiest option.

135
00:05:10,642 --> 00:05:12,450
Local buses also go there

136
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:15,163
but check Naver Map or KakaoMap for the

137
00:05:15,163 --> 00:05:16,124
current route.

138
00:05:16,124 --> 00:05:16,576
Later

139
00:05:16,576 --> 00:05:19,458
the subway makes the Haeundae-to-Centum City

140
00:05:19,458 --> 00:05:20,758
leg straightforward:

141
00:05:20,758 --> 00:05:22,623
it’s one stop on Line Two.

142
00:05:22,623 --> 00:05:26,014
Your transit card works on Busan buses and subway

143
00:05:26,014 --> 00:05:28,122
just as it does in Seoul.

144
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:30,387
Three easy mistakes to avoid:

145
00:05:30,387 --> 00:05:33,032
trying to cross all of Busan in one day

146
00:05:33,032 --> 00:05:34,990
leaving the temple until later

147
00:05:34,990 --> 00:05:37,846
and assuming you can get a sky-capsule ticket

148
00:05:37,846 --> 00:05:39,416
whenever you arrive.

149
00:05:39,834 --> 00:05:41,143
Busan is spread out

150
00:05:41,143 --> 00:05:43,970
so focus on the east coast instead of adding

151
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:44,913
distant sights.

152
00:05:44,913 --> 00:05:47,112
Going early helps with the temple’s

153
00:05:47,112 --> 00:05:48,263
mid-morning crowds

154
00:05:48,263 --> 00:05:51,405
and it leaves the beach for later in the morning.

155
00:05:51,405 --> 00:05:54,127
If you want the Blueline Park sky capsules

156
00:05:54,127 --> 00:05:56,326
plan ahead for summer and weekends

157
00:05:56,326 --> 00:05:58,002
when tickets can sell out.

158
00:05:58,002 --> 00:06:00,201
And don’t rely on old transport or

159
00:06:00,201 --> 00:06:01,667
opening-hour information:

160
00:06:01,667 --> 00:06:03,499
check a map app on the day

161
00:06:03,499 --> 00:06:06,574
especially for the temple route and the spa.

162
00:06:06,996 --> 00:06:10,236
Can you visit Busan as a day trip from Seoul?

163
00:06:10,236 --> 00:06:10,656
Yes

164
00:06:10,656 --> 00:06:12,296
the KTX makes it possible

165
00:06:12,296 --> 00:06:14,516
and the journey from Seoul Station to Busan

166
00:06:14,516 --> 00:06:17,356
Station takes about two and a half hours.

167
00:06:17,356 --> 00:06:19,656
But add about an hour to reach Haeundae from

168
00:06:19,656 --> 00:06:21,896
Busan Station by subway

169
00:06:21,896 --> 00:06:24,116
changing from Line One to Line Two.

170
00:06:24,116 --> 00:06:26,416
It makes for a long day.

171
00:06:26,416 --> 00:06:28,296
Staying at least one night

172
00:06:28,296 --> 00:06:29,576
ideally near Haeundae

173
00:06:29,576 --> 00:06:30,776
gives you more time.

174
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:34,876
What’s the easiest way to reach Haedong Yonggungsa?

175
00:06:34,876 --> 00:06:36,885
Take a taxi from Haeundae;

176
00:06:36,885 --> 00:06:39,710
allow around twenty to thirty minutes

177
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:41,279
depending on traffic.

178
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:42,911
Local buses also run.

179
00:06:42,911 --> 00:06:46,678
Check Naver Map or KakaoMap for the current route

180
00:06:46,678 --> 00:06:50,430
or show a taxi driver the Korean name, 해동용궁사.

181
00:06:50,808 --> 00:06:53,628
Does this plan work on a rainy day?

182
00:06:53,628 --> 00:06:54,468
Partly.

183
00:06:54,468 --> 00:06:55,868
The temple and beach are outdoors

184
00:06:55,868 --> 00:06:58,988
so those stops may be less comfortable in poor weather.

185
00:06:58,988 --> 00:07:02,048
The spa and Shinsegae Centum City are indoors

186
00:07:02,048 --> 00:07:04,488
so you can stretch out that part of the

187
00:07:04,488 --> 00:07:06,008
afternoon if the weather is bad.

188
00:07:06,522 --> 00:07:07,910
The plan is simple:

189
00:07:07,910 --> 00:07:10,223
start early at Haedong Yonggungsa

190
00:07:10,223 --> 00:07:13,693
return to Haeundae for the beach and market lunch

191
00:07:13,693 --> 00:07:16,989
then take Line Two to SPA LAND in Centum City.

192
00:07:16,989 --> 00:07:20,228
Come back for grilled ribs and a seaside walk.

193
00:07:20,228 --> 00:07:23,351
Add the Blueline Park only if you have time

194
00:07:23,351 --> 00:07:26,542
and consider Gwangalli for the night view.

195
00:07:27,036 --> 00:07:28,356
The full guide

196
00:07:28,356 --> 00:07:30,136
with links for every stop

197
00:07:30,136 --> 00:07:32,096
is on Korea Plainly.

198
00:07:32,096 --> 00:07:34,176
The link is in the description.

199
00:07:34,176 --> 00:07:35,676
If this helped

200
00:07:35,676 --> 00:07:37,276
subscribe for more plain

201
00:07:37,276 --> 00:07:38,536
practical guides to Korea.

